nd for continuity and  storyline purposes that probably  wouldn't work too well so it looks like  this is how it's going to go down we'll  get Spider-Man 4. this will most likely  address the events of what happened in  Spider-Man no way home with everybody  forgetting who Peter Parker was and of  course like I always mention keep in  mind people forgot who Peter Parker was  not Spider-Man so people still know who  Spider-Man is but there are big things  to address of course like will MJ and  Ned ever truly know their best friend  and love Peter Parker will doctor  strange and possibly Wong remember both  of them have already mentioned a  Spider-Man incident do they perhaps  remember that Peter Parker is Spider-Man  these are things that are going to have  to be addressed in Spider-Man 4  especially since Spider-Man is going to  be teaming up with the Avengers in the  next Spider-Man film appearance which is  going to be the King Dynasty so they're  going to kind of have to address the  whole identity thing beforehand  otherwise they'll have to spend time in  the King Dynasty explaining that in  which it seems like it's going to be a  pretty big movie and I'm not sure if  they're going to want to take that time  to explain that but then we'll have the  King Dynasty and Avenger Secret Wars and  this is where it gets really interesting  because Secret Wars I think is  essentially going to kind of reset the  MCU all the universes are going to  collide into one Universe we're going to  have a ton of different variants and I'm  assuming that somehow everything will  kind of get reset again to where the  Multiverse exists and there's a bunch of  different universes but I doubt  everything's just going to be completely  normal again so the MCU is going to be a  little bit different and possibly really  different after Secret Wars but the  coolest rumor that we've heard so far in  regards to Spider-Man and secret War is  that he is going to finally get the  Venom symbiote in secret Wars  now they tease the Venom symbiote in the  MCU in the post-credit scene for  Spider-Man no way home but rumors have  it that they want to wait till Secret  Wars to actually give him the Symbiote  because that is exactly what happens in  the comics where he wears the Venom  symbiote suit for the very first time in  secret Wars so I could definitely  appreciate a comic accurate story but if  that does happen that means that  Spider-Man 5 is going to be about Venom  and if they stay true to Comic accuracy  Peter Parker will obviously realize that  the Venom symbiote is not that good  he'll get rid of it and the Symbiote  will find Eddie Brock but at the same  time Kevin feige the president of Marvel  Studios doesn't like to do things that  have already been done before he likes  to shake it up which is why I do think  that him getting the symbiote suit in  secret Wars is pretty cool we haven't  seen that yet but will the next movie  have Eddie Brock in it that will remain  to be seen I think regardless he'll  eventually shake the suit and end up  fighting somebody who is wearing the  suit AKA Venom and I think that's pretty  much what Spider-Man 5 is going to be  about but if this truly is the final  deal for Tom Holland and the MCU like he  said he doesn't want to play Spider-Man  into his late 30s then that means sadly  Spider-Man 6 will most likely set up a  new Spider-Man now like I said there are  six different projects that apparently  he is signed for so one is unknown there  are conflicting reports right now  stating whether he could show up in  Daredevil or not one report that is  coming from the cosmic circus which  seems to be pretty accurate is that we  won't see Tom Holland show up in a  Disney Plus show this means he'll most  likely show up in another movie but if  this is truly Tom Holland's final deal  I'm assuming that Spider-Man 6 would  probably be his goodbye his own movie to  say goodbye in if Marvel is doing a  Young Avengers movie t